+\section{Prometheus and Grafana (1.6.4)}\label{sec:grafana}
+\subsection{Two ways to run the exporter}
+\begin{center}
+\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}p{0.22\linewidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}X@{}}
+\toprule
+Mode & How the values reach Grafana \\
+\midrule
+Continuous & poll every \code{--interval}; Prometheus pulls \code{/metrics}
+(job \code{ab_power_meter}), and/or every poll is pushed
+(\code{--push-gateway}, \code{--no-http}); \code{--count N} stops after $N$ polls \\
+Single run & \code{--once}: one poll pushed to a Pushgateway~\cite{prom_pushing},
+exit code 0 (a meter answered), 1 (none), 2 (push failed); run by a systemd
+timer or the Windows Task Scheduler \\
+Dict & \code{--print-json}: the dict as one JSON line per poll on stdout;
+from Python \code{poll_once()}, \code{iter_updates()}, \code{run(on_update=...)} \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabularx}
+\end{center}
+A push replaces the whole group \code{job/instance} (HTTP PUT)~\cite{prom_client_push},
+so a meter that stops answering disappears from it and \code{ab_meter_up}
+becomes 0. Pushes carry no timestamps (the Pushgateway rejects them) and no
+process counters. The exporter starts none of the monitor's writers and no
+log file, and sets \code{sys.dont_write_bytecode}; a test compares the program
+and working folders before and after a single run.
+
+\subsection{Dashboard}
+\code{ab_grafana_dashboard.py} takes the meters' dict --- from one headless
+poll, a running exporter, Prometheus' series API or a \code{--print-json} line
+--- and writes the dashboard JSON (schema 36, Grafana~9 and later)~\cite{grafana_json}:
+an Overview row, then one row per meter with one time-series panel per unit.
+Every parameter of a meter with the same unit is a trace of the same plot,
+selected by \code{ab_meter_value} with the meter's \code{ip} and the panel's
+\code{unit} label, so a panel picks up all series of its unit by itself.
+Panels with more than six traces span the full width with the legend on the
+right (Grafana gives a bottom legend only about a third of the panel height);
+values without a unit form a table. In the repeat layout a single row is
+repeated for every value of the \code{ip} variable; Grafana regex-escapes
+multi-value variables for Prometheus, so those panels match the IP with a
+regular expression (\code{=}\textasciitilde). Provisioning files and an upload
+through the HTTP API~\cite{grafana_provisioning,grafana_api} are included.
+
+\begin{figure}[htbp]
+  \centering
+  \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/grafana_dashboard.png}
+  \caption{Per-meter dashboard in Grafana 12.2 (emulated meters, 5\,s polls):
+  Overview row, then the voltage, current and power panels of the first meter.}
+  \label{fig:grafana}
+\end{figure}
+
+A Pushgateway keeps the last values until the next push, so \emph{Meter
+answering} is computed as
+\begin{equation}
+  u_\text{shown} = u \cdot
+  \bigl[\,t_\text{now} - t_\text{last poll} < t_\text{stale}\,\bigr],
+  \qquad t_\text{stale} = 3\,T,
+\end{equation}
+with $u$ the value of \code{ab_meter_up}, $[\cdot]$ = 1 when true and 0
+otherwise, and $T$ the poll or schedule period; it shows DOWN\,/\,STALE once
+the runs stop.
+
+\subsection{Python 3.7 on RHEL 9}
+RHEL~9's \code{python3} is 3.9 and it has no Python~3.7 package, so the
+interpreter comes from conda-forge (3.7.12). \code{install.sh} 1.2.0
+(\code{--mamba --py37}) creates it in \code{<prefix>/env} --- 1.1.0 used a named
+environment in root's home, which the service account cannot read and SELinux
+does not let services execute --- upgrades pip to 24.0 (the pip bundled with
+3.7 cannot read \code{manylinux_2_28} wheel tags), installs wheels only,
+labels the environment \code{bin_t} when SELinux is enabled, can open the
+exporter port in firewalld (\code{--open-port}) and installs the single-run
+timer (\code{--once-timer}). \code{prometheus_client} 0.17.1 and pip 24.0 are the
+last releases for Python~3.7. The unit files now keep \code{StartLimitBurst}
+and \code{StartLimitIntervalSec} in \code{[Unit]}; systemd~252 (RHEL~9)
+ignores the interval in \code{[Service]}.
+
+\subsection{Verification}
+Emulated meters, the exporter on Python~3.7.12, Prometheus~3.5.0,
+Pushgateway~1.11.1 and Grafana~12.2.0 (official binaries, checksums
+verified): 274 continuous polls, 68 single runs (all exit code 0), and the
+per-meter, repeat and API-uploaded dashboards rendered in headless Chromium
+with data in every panel and no browser errors. All pins of
+\code{requirements-py37.txt} installed as wheels on Python~3.7.12 and the
+monitor, exporter, dashboard and memory suites passed there and on 3.12.3.
+\code{install.sh --mamba --py37 --once-timer} ran end to end with a stubbed
+\code{systemctl}; every unit passes \code{systemd-analyze verify}. Not run: a
+real RHEL~9 host, so the SELinux and firewalld branches are unexercised.
+
